        >Maximum Compensable and Assessable Earnings (fact sheet WCB-615)</field>
        <field name="publisher">Workers' Compensation Board - Alberta</field>
        <field name="reference">Assessable earnings (PDF, January 1, 2026)</field>
        <field
            name="url"
        >https://www.wcb.ab.ca/assets/pdfs/employers/EFS_Maximum_compensable_and_assessable_earnings.pdf</field>
        <field
            name="summary"
        >Maximum assessable earnings (MAE) per worker: 106,400 in 2025, 110,900 in 2026; each worker's earnings are capped at the MAE before they are added to the total assessable earnings. MAE and maximum compensable earnings are set to cover the full wages of at least 90% of the workers of the province. Reissued near January 1.</field>
